    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outpu 1: E-services and Digital Centres established in pilot BARMM LGUs and Ministries and made accessible to women, senior citizens and PWDs 

1.1 Number of core ICT infrastructure (servers and data with software systems) for e-Governance established 
1.2 Number of project trained women with increased ICT capacities focused on management of Digital Centres and 
      Interactive Call Centres
1.3 Pool of trainers from LGUs, Ministries, CSOs for Empathy Training and Digital Service Design Lab established with at 
      least 50 percent women trainers
1.4 Number of individuals using Digital Centres and #DigitalBangsamoro portal (disaggregated by gender and marginalized 
      groups - PWD, SCs) 
1.5 Number of LGUs and BARMM ministry with updated Citizen&#x2019;s Charter (e-services integrated)

Output 2: BARMM local government units are able to collect gender-disaggregated household and sectoral data for use in 
local development and resilience planning.

2.1 Number of LGUs with increased capacities on DevLIVE+ data collection, management, and analysis, including gender- 
      sensitive data collection and analysis
2.2 Percentage of population of targeted barangays in BARMM  are recorded in the DevLIVE+ platform disaggregated by 
      sex
2.3 Number of government officials with increased understanding on evidence-based planning

Output 3: The 5-year Digital Transformation Roadmap for Bangsamoro is established with sustainability measures

3.1 Digital Transformation Roadmap published and endorsed by the MILG
3.2 Number of discussion papers on Digital Transformation taken up by the BARMM government 
3.3 Number of institutions, local and international, private, and public sectors included in a formal coalition to establish Digital 
      Bangsamoro
3.4 Number of developed operational modules and manuals 

Output 4: Program managed efficiently 
4.1 Regular meetings of Project Board convened with agreements acted in a timely manner
4.2 Percentage of quarterly targets achieved</narrative>
    </description>
